 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? It can be lot harder, especially with wind and cold. Many people stop riding altogether. Cover them lightly, not in a real cold spot. You can use finger gloves or whole gloves that cut away the layer between you and the box. Or a hood that zips up around your neck. That's a good compromise. The bus stays warm, and you don't have to worry about cold hands. Touring tyres with good grip and some puncture resistance are worth having, even on short trips. You' be glad you have them.",
